        <mxCell id="note" value="First-apply facts baked in: credential providers use client_authentication_method (the old token_endpoint_auth_methods is refused); Gateway with an IAM authorizer refuses 3LO targets, so number-verification is not registered and the binding page does its own auth-code exchange (binding_carrier_client = &quot;direct&quot;, which needs the NAT); AgentCore creates the runtime log groups itself; Runtime does not inject AWS_REGION; on-demand Nova needs the us.* inference profile; a new account's Bedrock daily token quota is 0, hence the cross-account role." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=10;fontColor=#6B7A90;fontStyle=0;spacing=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
